Fixed. The bug was a `break` statement inside the tracking-param loop in `src/url_utils.ts` — it stopped after stripping the first matching parameter, leaving any subsequent ones (e.g. `fbclid` when `utm_source` was also present) in the URL.

Removed the `break`, so all parameters in `TRACKING_PARAMS` that are present get stripped. Verified with a test: `https://example.com/page?utm_source=google&fbclid=abc123` now correctly normalizes to `https://example.com/page`, and the same for a URL with `utm_source` + `utm_medium`.


